                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A009" OID="5883b506-9ab3-40cd-a518-4bef6f811757">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A009</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6397961</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A009</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_857635472">Radar Module -Front center (MRR) - Component Failure</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1167444379">NO Service Relevant</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_208831003">- EC2: Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V) &amp;&amp; EC4: De-bounce timer</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_263492178">65 msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_207897432">The Hydra3_component shall log the DTC if any one of the following conditions is met -  1. RADAR_INFO (0x300)||OBJ_DATA_00 (0x310)||OBJ_DATA_01 (0x311)||OBJ_DATA_02 (0x312)||OBJ_DATA_03 (0x313)||OBJ_DATA_04 (0x314)||OBJ_DATA_05 (0x315)||OBJ_DATA_06 (0x316)||OBJ_DATA_07 (0x317)||OBJ_DATA_08 (0x318)||OBJ_DATA_09 (0x319)||OBJ_DATA_10 (0x31A)||OBJ_DATA_11 (0x31B)||OBJ_DATA_12 (0x31C)||OBJ_DATA_13 (0x31D)||OBJ_DATA_14 (0x31E)||OBJ_DATA_15 (0x31F)||OBJ_DATA_16 (0x320)||OBJ_DATA_17 (0x321)||OBJ_DATA_18 (0x322)||OBJ_DATA_19 (0x323)||OBJ_DATA_20 (0x324)||OBJ_DATA_21 (0x325)||OBJ_DATA_22 (0x326)||OBJ_DATA_23 (0x327)||OBJ_DATA_24 (0x328)||OBJ_DATA_25 (0x329)||OBJ_DATA_26 (0x32A)||OBJ_DATA_27 (0x32B)||OBJ_DATA_28 (0x32C)||OBJ_DATA_29 (0x32D)||OBJ_DATA_30 (0x32E)||OBJ_DATA_31 (0x32F)||ROAD_BORDER (0x500) message missing for 650 msec OR 2. RADAR_CFG (0x600) message missing for 10 sec OR 3. Hydra3 receives SensorStatus - 0x7 (SENSOR_ST_EXTERNAL_ERROR) from RADAR_INFO (0x300) message and it is valid for 650 msec OR 4. After setting any of the below NRCs, the diagnostic tool will re-attempt (3 times) to flash MRR through Hydra3 and fails a. Subfunction not supported ($12) b. Incorrect message/data length or invalid format ($13) c. Flashing conditions not correct (vehicle speed/ECU voltage) ($22) d.  Incorrect sequence ($24) e.  Request out of range ($31) f. Security Access denied ($33) g. General Programming Failure ($72) OR 5. Re-flashing halts or aborts programming midway- MRR accepts the reprogramming request, but during the flash, the software suddenly halts and installation is incomplete. OR 6. Flashing is complete, but MRR malfunctions due to error in software OR 7. For the message RADAR_INFO (0x300)||OBJ_DATA_00 (0x310)||OBJ_DATA_01 (0x311)||OBJ_DATA_02 (0x312)||OBJ_DATA_03 (0x313)||OBJ_DATA_04 (0x314)||OBJ_DATA_05 (0x315)||OBJ_DATA_06 (0x316)||OBJ_DATA_07 (0x317)||OBJ_DATA_08 (0x318)||OBJ_DATA_09 (0x319)||OBJ_DATA_10 (0x31A)||OBJ_DATA_11 (0x31B)||OBJ_DATA_12 (0x31C)||OBJ_DATA_13 (0x31D)||OBJ_DATA_14 (0x31E)||OBJ_DATA_15 (0x31F)||OBJ_DATA_16 (0x320)||OBJ_DATA_17 (0x321)||OBJ_DATA_18 (0x322)||OBJ_DATA_19 (0x323)||OBJ_DATA_20 (0x324)||OBJ_DATA_21 (0x325)||OBJ_DATA_22 (0x326)||OBJ_DATA_23 (0x327)||OBJ_DATA_24 (0x328)||OBJ_DATA_25 (0x329)||OBJ_DATA_26 (0x32A)||OBJ_DATA_27 (0x32B)||OBJ_DATA_28 (0x32C)||OBJ_DATA_29 (0x32D)||OBJ_DATA_30 (0x32E)||OBJ_DATA_31 (0x32F)||ROAD_BORDER (0x500)||RADAR_CFG (0x600), if - CRC verification error occurs in the last 3 consecutive messages OR - Maximum difference of Counter value (MaxDeltaCounterInit) &gt; 1 for 3 times continuously OR - Counter value is repeated in the last 3 consecutive messages OR - MAC verification error occurs in the last 3 consecutive messages 

OR 
8. Front Center MRR role and scan config is incorrect during start up i.e. Hydra3 receives RadarRoleConfig != 0x1 (RadarRoleConfig_ROLE_FRONT) from message RADAR_CFG (0x600) during Start up via HSCAN2. 
OR 
9. Hydra3 receives MRRTimesyncStatus = 0x0 (MRRTimesyncStatus_TSYNC_NOT_SYNCED) || 0x3 ( 
MRRTimesyncStatus_TSYNC_SNA) from RADAR_INFO (0x300) message and it is valid for 650 msec.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_2108053120">Hydra3_component shall not log any DTC if all the conditions below are True-  1. Received lost messages from the MRR node and valid for 650 msec (Except RADAR_CFG (0x600) message is valid for 10 sec) AND 2. Hydra3 receives SensorStatus - 0x0 (SENSOR_ST_INIT) || 0x1 (SENSOR_ST_NORMAL) || 0x9 ( SENSOR_ST_SCAN_DISABLED) from message RADAR_INFO (0x300) and it is valid for 650 msec. AND 3. Flash/re-flash is successful AND 4. No CRC, MAC, Message Counter error (All signal values are valid) and last for 1 cycle. 
AND 
5. Hydra3 receives RadarRoleConfig = 0x1 (RadarRoleConfig_ROLE_FRONT) from message RADAR_CFG (0x600) during Start up via HSCAN2 
AND 
6. Hydra3 receives MRRTimesyncStatus = 0x1 (MRRTimesyncStatus_TSYNC_SYNCED) from RADAR_INFO (0x300) message and it is valid for 650 msec.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_243990967">Following features will not be available:  Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA), Personal Park Assist, Remote Parking Assist 

Following Feature will be degraded : 
Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1711446047">- Harness defect - MRR Sensor defect</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_992213210">Features that rely on MRR will stop functioning or degrade</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A109" OID="1df8f23c-674a-461a-9b4a-ecb51ec4fa42">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A109</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6398217</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A109</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_685764602">Rear Camera - Component Failure</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1167444379">NO Service Relevant</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1184074624">1. Check Harness 2. Ensure correct camera functionality 3. Restart the system</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_269786807">EC 1- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)   
EC 2- BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)
EC 3-  BUS physical status  
EC 4- De-bounce timer </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_283828234">100 msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1617302649">The Hydra3_Component shall set the DTC if any one of the following criteria is met: 1. Open circuit/Short to battery failure if IN3 = L , Fault = L for 500 ms  OR 2. Short to ground failure if IN3 = H, Fault = L for 500 ms Note : Depending upon the status of INx and Fault line, chip can read the failure. Refer to Hydra3 schematic diagram and HSIS documenttaion for the meaning of INx and Fault pins. SoC is going to determine the state of the Pins using its Video - In schematic block connection. For Rear camera, x = 3. So Channel 3 from CAM_CS_A is selected i.e. CAM3_PWR_EN is enabled for rear camera.  OR 3. Thermal shutdown to occur if temperature reading is more than 125 deg C for 500 ms Note: The Register Address of the temperature sensor is R0x3E9A (Refer to developer's guide for AR0233AT Image Sensor: Section - Temperature Sensor)  OR 4. Lock failure on deserializer side for 500 ms. OR 5. Not receiving any image, images are frozen, images are not being refreshed for 500ms OR 6. CRC Error (Read thru register over I2C) OR 7.  Calibration data is not configured/Alignment is Incorrect or not completed OR 8. Calibration data cannot be read from the flash</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_59676079">Hydra3_component shall not log any DTC if all the conditions below are True - 1. Rear camera is connected, No power supply error and current (CAM_CS_A) is within limit (70-250 mA) for 1 secs AND 2. Imager temperature is within limit (-40 to 125 degree C) and valid for 1 secs AND 3. No lock failure AND 4. no flicker, Fresh Images are received/displayed on the screen AND 5. No CRC Error AND 6. Calibration is successful and Calibration and data identified as correct/valid</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1687207215">- Output Video:  Rear Video feed grayed out in all Views (Rear view, Rear cross path view, Free floating view)  - Features Not available: i. Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Rear Automatic Emergency Braking: RAEB ii. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) iii. Personal Park Assist iv. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_715648373">1. Harness defect 2. Camera defect 3. Camera is not powered as specified by ECU</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_630212688">- Views will be blanked: Rear view, Rear cross path view, Free floating view - Features that rely on Rear Camera will be unavailable</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A209" OID="53e414da-8e76-4392-b30e-2499cddab4cf">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A209</SHORT-NAME>
