                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_269786807">EC 1- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)   
EC 2- BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)
EC 3-  BUS physical status  
EC 4- De-bounce timer </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_283828234">100 msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_741922487">The Hydra3_Component shall set the DTC if any one of the following criteria is met: 1. Open circuit/Short to battery failure if IN2 = L , Fault = L for 500 ms  OR 2. Short to ground failure if IN2 = H, Fault = L for 500 ms Note : Depending upon the status of INx and Fault line, chip can read the failure. Refer to Hydra3 schematic diagram and HSIS documenttaion for the meaning of INx and Fault pins. SoC is going to determine the state of the Pins using its 'Video - In' schematic block connection. For Left side camera, x = 2. So Channel 2 from CAM_CS_A is selected i.e. CAM2_PWR_EN is enabled for Left side camera.  OR 3. Thermal shutdown occurs if temperature reading is more than 125 deg C for 500 ms Note: The Register Address of the temperature sensor is R0x3E9A (Refer to developer's guide for AR0233AT Image Sensor: Section - Temperature Sensor)  OR 4. Lock failure on deserializer side for 500 ms. OR 5. Not receiving any image, images are frozen, images are not being refreshed for 500ms OR 6. CRC Error (Read thru register over I2C) OR 7.  Calibration data is not configured/Alignment is Incorrect or not completed OR 8. Calibration data cannot be read from the flash</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_654440480">Hydra3_component shall not log any DTC if all the conditions below are True - 1. Left camera is connected, No power supply error and current (CAM_CS_A) is within limit (70-250 mA) for 1 sec AND 2. Imager temperature is within limit (-40 to 125 degree C) and valid for 1 sec AND 3. No lock failure AND 4. No flicker, Fresh images are received/displayed on the screen AND 5. No CRC Error AND 6. Calibration is successful and Calibration data identified as correct/valid</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_516965126">- Output Video:  Left camera video feed grayed out in all Views (Curb view, left flank 3D view, free floating view)  - Features Not available: i. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) ii. Personal Park Assist iii. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_715648373">1. Harness defect 2. Camera defect 3. Camera is not powered as specified by ECU</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_334751899">- Views will be blanked: Left side videos, Left Side split (curb) view and Left flank 3D view, free floating view - Features that rely on Left Camera will be unavailable</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
