                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_269786807">EC 1- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)   
EC 2- BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)
EC 3-  BUS physical status  
EC 4- De-bounce timer </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_283828234">100 msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1677727409">The Hydra3_Component shall set the DTC if any one of the following criteria is met: 1. Open circuit/Short to battery failure if IN1 = L , Fault = L for 500 ms  OR 2. Short to ground failure if IN1 = H, Fault = L for 500 ms Note : Depending upon the status of INx and Fault line, chip can read the failure. Refer to Hydra3 schematic diagram and HSIS documenttaion for the meaning of INx and Fault pins. SoC is going to determine the state of the Pins using its 'Video - In' schematic block connection. For Right side camera, x = 1. So Channel 1 from CAM_CS_A is selected i.e. CAM1_PWR_EN is enabled for Right side camera.  OR 3. Thermal shutdown occurs if temperature reading is more than 125 deg C for 500 ms Note: The Register Address of the temperature sensor is R0x3E9A (Refer to developer's guide for AR0233AT Image Sensor: Section - Temperature Sensor)  OR 4. Lock failure on deserializer side for 500 ms. OR 5. Not receiving any image, images are frozen, images are not being refreshed for 500ms OR 6. CRC Error (Read thru register over I2C) OR 7.  Calibration data is not configured/Alignment is Incorrect or not completed OR 8. Calibration data cannot be read from the flash</SD>
