                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A609" OID="e5c58842-335b-416c-a4c0-3c7a06b949d5">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A609</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6399497</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A609</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_909574872">DMS camera Component failure</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1167444379">NO Service Relevant</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_292584841"/>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_283828234">100 msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1854475379">The Hydra3_Component shall set the DTC if any one of the following criteria is met:
 1. Open circuit/Short to battery failure if IN1 = L (CAM_BANK_B), Fault = L for 500 ms OR 2. Short to ground failure if IN1 = H (CAM_BANK_B), Fault = L for 500 ms
 Note : Depending upon the status of INx and Fault line, chip can read the failure. Refer to Hydra3 schematic diagram and HSIS documenttaion for the meaning of INx and Fault pins. SoC is going to determine the state of the Pins using its 'Video - In' schematic block connection. For DMS camera, x = 1 and Channel 5 from CAM_CS_B is selected i.e. CAM5_PWR_EN is enabled for DMS camera. 

OR 
 The Hydra3_component shall log the DTC if it receives any one of the following Flags from DMS camera (OV2311) and the flag is present for 500 ms :
 1. status 
OR 
2. fail_safe 
OR 
3. temperature 
OR 
4. frame_counter
OR
5. i2C_communication</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_654440480">Hydra3_component shall not log any DTC if all the conditions below are True - 1. Left camera is connected, No power supply error and current (CAM_CS_A) is within limit (70-250 mA) for 1 sec AND 2. Imager temperature is within limit (-40 to 125 degree C) and valid for 1 sec AND 3. No lock failure AND 4. No flicker, Fresh images are received/displayed on the screen AND 5. No CRC Error AND 6. Calibration is successful and Calibration data identified as correct/valid</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_2024996780"> Features Not Available - 
1. Driver drowsiness warning and 
2. Driver attention warning.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_715648373">1. Harness defect 2. Camera defect 3. Camera is not powered as specified by ECU</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_100180444"> Unavailability of Driver drowsiness warning and Driver attention warning.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A709" OID="d1f8e7bd-4e17-468d-84b6-28e02d93bf86">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A709</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6399753</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A709</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1296359957">DMS IR LED Driver component Failure</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1167444379">NO Service Relevant</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_337485890">EC 1- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)   
EC 2- BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)
EC 3-  BUS physical status  
EC 4- De-bounce timer</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_283828234">100 msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1574481541">The Hydra3_component shall log the DTC if it receives any one of the following Flags from DMS IR LED Driver (MAX25614AB) and the flag is present for 500 ms :
 1. status 
OR 
2. temperature 
OR 
3. i2C_communication</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1231295473">Hydra3_component shall not log any DTC if No error flag received for 1 sec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_123662442">Features Not Available - 
1. Driver drowsiness warning and 
2. Driver attention warning.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1887562465">1. Harness defect 2. IR LED defect 3. IR LED is not powered as specified by ECU 4. IR LED disconnected</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1509476006">Unavailability of Driver drowsiness warning and Driver attention warning.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A855" OID="0d653c85-5c15-468f-85a7-d09863ac8c18">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A855</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6400085</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A855</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1265735836">ADAS DC is not coded with Coding data string (CDS)</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1732356815">Service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1685949360">- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)  - BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)  - BUS physical status  - De-bounce timer </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1068755964">At Start up (During Post Coding process)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_124886643">The Hydra3_component shall set the DTC Immediately if it receives -CodingStateFlag = NotCoded</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_2087615381">The Hydra3_component shall not set this DTC if the CodingStateFlag = CodingValid OR CodingInvalid</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_270997218">For High-Speed Safety features:  FID_AEB_Low_Impact FID_VRU_Low_Impact FID_SCP_Low_Impact FID_RCTAB_Medium_Impact FID_LTAP_Low_Impact FID_ESA_Low_Impact  FID_LKA_Low_Impact  For the definition of above limp-home actions, refer to Requirement 16315106    Features that are in error state/Not available/Deactivated: 1. Lane Change Assist (LCA) 2. Traffic jam assist (TJA) 3. Integrated Cruise Assist (ICA) 4. Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go 
5. Door Opening Incident Warning (DOIW)  6. Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Rear Automatic Emergency Braking: RAEB 7. Wheel scratch-prevention Parking Assist  (WSP) 8. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) 9. Personal Park Assist 10. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1590924323">ECU is a new one and going to be mounted on the vehicle first time, including ECU replacement in After Sales/service.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_528401642">1. Low speed safety features will not be available 2. Except Auto High Beam (AHB), Intelligent Speed Assist (ISA), Blind Spot Monitoring (BSM) and Traffic Sign/Light Recognition (TSLR), other comfort features will not be available. AHB, ISA, BSM and TSLR will be in normal operation. 3. Low impact degradation for high-speed safety features.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A856" OID="53bdcb5a-4662-421e-9cc5-4798b4863a71">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A856</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6400086</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A856</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2069424663">ADAS DC with Invalid Coding </TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1732356815">Service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1685949360">- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)  - BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)  - BUS physical status  - De-bounce timer </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1566524128">During Start up/coding process</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_2064520538">The Hydra3_component shall set the DTC if it receives:  CodingStateFlag = codingInvalid OR CodingNotChecked.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1888451195">The Hydra3_component shall not set this DTC if the CodingStateFlag = CodingValid OR NotCoded</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_270997218">For High-Speed Safety features:  FID_AEB_Low_Impact FID_VRU_Low_Impact FID_SCP_Low_Impact FID_RCTAB_Medium_Impact FID_LTAP_Low_Impact FID_ESA_Low_Impact  FID_LKA_Low_Impact  For the definition of above limp-home actions, refer to Requirement 16315106    Features that are in error state/Not available/Deactivated: 1. Lane Change Assist (LCA) 2. Traffic jam assist (TJA) 3. Integrated Cruise Assist (ICA) 4. Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go 
5. Door Opening Incident Warning (DOIW)  6. Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Rear Automatic Emergency Braking: RAEB 7. Wheel scratch-prevention Parking Assist  (WSP) 8. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) 9. Personal Park Assist 10. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1710625278">1. CRC error 2.  Data length error 3. Short VIN mismatch 4.  Memory (NVM) is not sufficient to store the CDS</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_528401642">1. Low speed safety features will not be available 2. Except Auto High Beam (AHB), Intelligent Speed Assist (ISA), Blind Spot Monitoring (BSM) and Traffic Sign/Light Recognition (TSLR), other comfort features will not be available. AHB, ISA, BSM and TSLR will be in normal operation. 3. Low impact degradation for high-speed safety features.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCC21A909" OID="fddd7e6e-4558-43d7-b0a8-8811463a4d65">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A909</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6400265</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A909</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_857635472">Radar Module -Front center (MRR) - Component Failure</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1540890856">No service</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_809402428">EC 1- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)   
EC 2- BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)
EC 3-  BUS physical status 
EC 4- De-bounce timer
- Hydra3 has not requested the MRR to go into Low power mode.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1340650257">Continue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_592668466">20ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1732729024">The Hydra3_component shall log the DTC if any one of the following conditions is met -  1. RADAR_INFO (0x300)||OBJ_DATA_00 (0x310)||OBJ_DATA_01 (0x311)||OBJ_DATA_02 (0x312)||OBJ_DATA_03 (0x313)||OBJ_DATA_04 (0x314)||OBJ_DATA_05 (0x315)||OBJ_DATA_06 (0x316)||OBJ_DATA_07 (0x317)||OBJ_DATA_08 (0x318)||OBJ_DATA_09 (0x319)||OBJ_DATA_10 (0x31A)||OBJ_DATA_11 (0x31B)||OBJ_DATA_12 (0x31C)||OBJ_DATA_13 (0x31D)||OBJ_DATA_14 (0x31E)||OBJ_DATA_15 (0x31F)||OBJ_DATA_16 (0x320)||OBJ_DATA_17 (0x321)||OBJ_DATA_18 (0x322)||OBJ_DATA_19 (0x323)||OBJ_DATA_20 (0x324)||OBJ_DATA_21 (0x325)||OBJ_DATA_22 (0x326)||OBJ_DATA_23 (0x327)||OBJ_DATA_24 (0x328)||OBJ_DATA_25 (0x329)||OBJ_DATA_26 (0x32A)||OBJ_DATA_27 (0x32B)||OBJ_DATA_28 (0x32C)||OBJ_DATA_29 (0x32D)||OBJ_DATA_30 (0x32E)||OBJ_DATA_31 (0x32F)||ROAD_BORDER (0x500)||RADAR_STATE (0x301)||
RADAR_CFG (0x600) message missing for 200 msec 
3. Hydra3 receives SensorStatus - 0x7 (SENSOR_ST_EXTERNAL_ERROR) from RADAR_STATE (0x301) message and it is valid for 200 msec
4. For the message RADAR_INFO (0x300)||OBJ_DATA_00 (0x310)||OBJ_DATA_01 (0x311)||OBJ_DATA_02 (0x312)||OBJ_DATA_03 (0x313)||OBJ_DATA_04 (0x314)||OBJ_DATA_05 (0x315)||OBJ_DATA_06 (0x316)||OBJ_DATA_07 (0x317)||OBJ_DATA_08 (0x318)||OBJ_DATA_09 (0x319)||OBJ_DATA_10 (0x31A)||OBJ_DATA_11 (0x31B)||OBJ_DATA_12 (0x31C)||OBJ_DATA_13 (0x31D)||OBJ_DATA_14 (0x31E)||OBJ_DATA_15 (0x31F)||OBJ_DATA_16 (0x320)||OBJ_DATA_17 (0x321)||OBJ_DATA_18 (0x322)||OBJ_DATA_19 (0x323)||OBJ_DATA_20 (0x324)||OBJ_DATA_21 (0x325)||OBJ_DATA_22 (0x326)||OBJ_DATA_23 (0x327)||OBJ_DATA_24 (0x328)||OBJ_DATA_25 (0x329)||OBJ_DATA_26 (0x32A)||OBJ_DATA_27 (0x32B)||OBJ_DATA_28 (0x32C)||OBJ_DATA_29 (0x32D)||OBJ_DATA_30 (0x32E)||OBJ_DATA_31 (0x32F)||ROAD_BORDER (0x500)||RADAR_STATE (0x301)||RADAR_CFG (0x600), if - CRC verification error occurs in the last 3 consecutive messages OR - Maximum difference of Counter value (MaxDeltaCounterInit) &gt; 1 for 3 times continuously OR - Counter value is repeated in the last 3 consecutive messages OR - MAC verification error occurs in the last 3 consecutive messages 

OR 
5. Front Center MRR role and scan config is incorrect during start up i.e. Hydra3 receives RadarRoleConfig != 0x1 (RadarRoleConfig_ROLE_FRONT) from message RADAR_CFG (0x600) during Start up via HSCAN2. 
OR 
6. Hydra3 receives MRRTimesyncStatus = 0x0 (MRRTimesyncStatus_TSYNC_NOT_SYNCED) || 0x3 ( 
MRRTimesyncStatus_TSYNC_SNA) from RADAR_INFO (0x300) message and it is valid for 650 msec.  
OR 
7. Hydra3 receives SensorStatus - 0xC (SENSOR_ST_SAFETY_ERROR) from RADAR_STATE (0x301) message and it is valid for 200 msec </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1706424208">Hydra3_component shall not log any DTC if all the conditions below are True-  1. Received lost messages from the MRR node and valid for 200 msec
2. Hydra3 receives SensorStatus - 0x0 (SENSOR_ST_INIT) || 0x1 (SENSOR_ST_NORMAL) || 0x9 ( SENSOR_ST_SCAN_DISABLED) from message RADAR_STATE (0x301) and it is valid for 200 msec.  AND 3. Flash/re-flash is successful AND 4. No CRC, MAC, Message Counter error (All signal values are valid) and last for 1 cycle. 
AND 
5. Hydra3 receives RadarRoleConfig = 0x1 (RadarRoleConfig_ROLE_FRONT) from message RADAR_CFG (0x600) during Start up via HSCAN2 
AND 
6. Hydra3 receives MRRTimesyncStatus = 0x1 (MRRTimesyncStatus_TSYNC_SYNCED) from RADAR_INFO (0x300) message and it is valid for 650 msec.  </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_680977892">- Features in error state :  Lane change assist (LCA)  - Features degraded :  Traffic jam assist (TJA) / Integrated Cruise Assist (ICA)/ Lane Centering Control (LCC), Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go    - Low critical degradation if following features are engaged : Automatic Emergency Braking - Standard Car2Car (Inlcuding Following and HeadOn): AEB-C2C, Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Turn Across Path Vehicle Collision Mitigation: AEB-TAP, Automatic Emergency Braking - Standard Forward Pedestrian Collision Mitigation: AEB-VRU, Automatic Emergency Braking - Standard Forward Cyclist Collision Mitigation: AEB-Cyc  - High critical degradation if following features are disengaged :  Automatic Emergency Braking - Standard Car2Car (Inlcuding Following and HeadOn): AEB-C2C, Automatic Emergency Braking - Standard Forward Pedestrian Collision Mitigation: AEB-VRU, Automatic Emergency Braking - Standard Forward Cyclist Collision Mitigation: AEB-Cyc, Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Turn Across Path Vehicle Collision Mitigation: AEB-TAP  - Low critical degradation if following features are engaged/Dis-engaged :  Emergency Lane Departure Avoidance (ELDA)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1711446047">- Harness defect - MRR Sensor defect</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_992213210">Features that rely on MRR will stop functioning or degrade</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
