                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC21B000">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21B000</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6402048</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21B000</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_430847432">Symmetric key for SecOC (also known as Key-Raw) is set to default/initial value</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_781636891">Check at next stop</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1306322628">Enter the new key</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_292584841"/>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_689504060">
On - Demand</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_858292156">During Start up</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_30844976">The Hydra3_component shall set the DTC Immediately if the Symmetric key for SecOC value is set to Default or initial value (All 16 bytes are filled with FF) </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_196174690">The Hydra3_component shall not set the DTC if the Symmetric key for SecOC value is written correctly</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1353507680">For High-Speed Safety features:   FID_AEB_Critical_Impact FID_VRU_Critical_Impact FID_SCP_Critical_Impact FID_RCTAB_Critical_Impact FID_LTAP_Critical_Impact FID_ESA_Critical_Impact FID_LKA_Critical_Impact  For the definition of above limp-home actions, refer to 
Requirement 16315106  

Features that are in error state/Not available/Deactivated: All the comfort features and low speed safety features will be unavailable.   Comfort and low speed safety Feature List - 1. Lane Change Assist (LCA) 2. Traffic jam assist (TJA) 3. Integrated Cruise Assist (ICA) 4. Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go 5. Auto High Beam (AHB) 6. Intelligent Speed Assist (ISA) 7. Blind Spot Monitoring (BSM) 8. Traffic Sign/Light Recognition (TSLR) 9. Door Opening Incident Warning (DOIW)   10. Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Rear Automatic Emergency Braking: RAEB 11. Wheel scratch-prevention Parking Assist (WSP) 12. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) 13. Personal Park Assist 14. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_491091207">40 Drive Cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1831454613">
No key is written / correct keys are not written onto the ECU.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_76930812">Failure in key distribution process will result into fail secoc</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC21B142">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21B142</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6402370</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21B142</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_998714458">Failure to Read - Write Symmetric Key for SecOC from/onto ECU Memory</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>1</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1732356815">Service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1988258738">
1. Check memory status</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_292584841"/>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_510928239">
10 ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1648077098">The Hydra3_component shall set the DTC if - It can't read the symmetric key for SecOC (DID 0xEFF5) from ADAS DC memory (NVM/key storage area) OR Not able to Write the symmetric key onto ADAS DC memory.,The Hydra3_component shall not set the DTC if the ECU is able to read and write the key successfully from its memory</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_725032003">For High-Speed Safety features:   FID_AEB_Critical_Impact FID_VRU_Critical_Impact FID_SCP_Critical_Impact FID_RCTAB_Critical_Impact FID_LTAP_Critical_Impact FID_ESA_Critical_Impact FID_LKA_Critical_Impact  For the definition of above limp-home actions, refer to 
Requirement 16315106  

Features that are in error state/Not available/Deactivated: All the comfort features and low speed safety features will be unavailable.   Comfort and low speed safety Feature List - 1. Lane Change Assist (LCA) 2. Traffic jam assist (TJA) 3. Integrated Cruise Assist (ICA) 4. Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go 5. Auto High Beam (AHB) 6. Intelligent Speed Assist (ISA) 7. Blind Spot Monitoring (BSM) 8. Traffic Sign/Light Recognition (TSLR) 9. Door Opening Incident Warning (DOIW)   10. Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Rear Automatic Emergency Braking: RAEB 11. Wheel scratch-prevention Parking Assist (WSP) 12. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) 13. Personal Park Assist 14. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_983679744">40 Drive cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1671649666">memory corruption issue</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1046081346">
Unable to provide status of defualt key and unable to write symmetric key in NVM</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_11679372">Unable to provide status of defualt key and unable to write symmetric key in NVM</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC21B200">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21B200</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6402560</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21B200</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1642468404">ADAS DC Secure Protocol Data Unit (PDU) Authentication Fail</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>1</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1732356815">Service immediately</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_292584841"/>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_563597339">Failure to authenticate at any time (Need to update the rate based on secured pdu verification time)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1950213174">The Hydra3_component shall set the DTC If - Freshness value (FV) synchronization message verification fails OR - Abnormal freshness value synchronization message is received.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_2055408849">The Hydra3_component shall not set any DTC If the secured PDU authentication is successful.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1039781787">For High-Speed Safety features:   FID_AEB_Critical_Impact FID_VRU_Critical_Impact FID_SCP_Critical_Impact FID_RCTAB_Critical_Impact FID_LTAP_Critical_Impact FID_ESA_Critical_Impact FID_LKA_Critical_Impact  For the definition of above limp-home actions, refer to Requirement 16315106   Features that are in error state/Not available/Deactivated: All the comfort features and low speed safety features will be unavailable.   Comfort and low speed safety Feature List - 1. Lane Change Assist (LCA) 2. Traffic jam assist (TJA) 3. Integrated Cruise Assist (ICA) 4. Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go 5. Auto High Beam (AHB) 6. Intelligent Speed Assist (ISA) 7. Blind Spot Monitoring (BSM) 8. Traffic Sign/Light Recognition (TSLR) 9. Door Opening Incident Warning (DOIW)   10. Automatic Emergency Braking - Premium Rear Automatic Emergency Braking: RAEB 11. Wheel scratch-prevention Parking Assist  (WSP) 12. Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA) 13. Personal Park Assist 14. Remote Parking Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_983679744">40 Drive cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1737397428">FV synchronization message will be dropped</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC219E09">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC219E09</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6397449</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C219E09</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_843910373">USS - Front Inner Right (FIR) Sensor Component Failure</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_781636891">Check at next stop</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_806402071">1. Check connectors 2. Check FIR sensor 3. Disconnect and re-connect FIR sensor 4. Ensure stable power supply to Front USS sensor 5. If problem still exists, replace FIL sensor</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_356741382">EC-1 Ignition status &amp;&amp; EC-2 Local Voltage &amp;&amp; EC-4 De-bounce time </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1343099799">
100 ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_886988114">The Hydra3_component shall log the DTC if it receives any one of the following Flags from FIR sensor and flag present for 400 ms: 
 1. FIR_hardware_Fault OR 2. FIR_OverTemp_fault OR 3. FIR_comm_Fault OR 4. FIR_CommUnknown OR 5. FIR_SNR_Firmware_Mismatch OR 6. FIR_Blockage</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_245832471">
No error flag received for 1 sec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1217555270">
Following features will not be available:  Full Automatic Park Assist System (APA), Personal Park Assist, Remote Parking Assist 

Following Feature will be degraded : 
Automatic Cruise Control (ACC) Including Stop and Go</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_983679744">40 Drive cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_388601090">Failure in the power supply chain/connection error</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1813306083">Parking Feature unavailable</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC21A531">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A531</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6399281</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A531</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1113528206">FCM Sensor Failure - Loss of communication, Timeout of ethernet bus</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_781636891">Check at next stop</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_617985664">Ensure stable ethernet connection</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_292584841"/>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_73335078">50ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_18192328">Hydra3_component shall set a DTC If any one of the below PDUs which FCM sends to Hydra3 is missed for 500 ms (10 * cycle rate of each PDU i.e. 50 ms) 
 - Light_Scene_Boundle_PDU - Objects_Boundle_PDU - Road_Boundle_PDU - TFL_Boundle_PDU - TSR_Boundle_PDU - Core_Objects_protocol_1024 - Core_Objects_protocol_1025 </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_841449077">All the PDU messages that FCM sends to Hydra3 are received and valid for 1 sec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1376656762">FID_LCA_Critical_Impact FID_LCC_Critical_Impact FID_AHB_Critical_Impact FID_ACC_High_Impact FID_ISA_Critical_Impact FID_TSR_Critical_Impact FID_TLR_Critical_Impact FID_AEB_FCW_Medium FID_VRU_FCW_Medium FID_LTAP_FCW_Medium FID_ESA_Critical_Impact FID_LKA_Critical_Impact FID_LCW_Critical_Impact</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_983679744">40 Drive cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1130416441">Interruption on ethernet communication lines OR Ethernet connection is not established within t msec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_253719004">Features that rely on FCM data are not functioning or degraded</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC21A586">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21A586</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6399366</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21A586</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_263812975">Hydra3 - FCM Communication Verification failure</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1537941729">
Check at next stop</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_818474858">1. Reconnect the battery 2. Ensure correct Ethernet functionality 3. Check the ECUs (ADAS DC and FCM)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1201259791"> - Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)  - BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)  - BUS physical status  - De-bounce timer</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1242778992">
50 ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1272500164">
Hydra3_Component shall set the DTC for any one of the below signals, 
 - Light_Scene_Boundle_PDU OR - Objects_Boundle_PDU OR - Road_Boundle_PDU OR - TFL_Boundle_PDU OR - TSR_Boundle_PDU OR - Core_Objects_protocol OR - Ethernet_FUSA_PDU  If  --&gt; Check Sum verification error occurs in the last 3 consecutive signals OR --&gt; Maximum difference of Counter value (MaxDeltaCounterInit) &gt; 1 for 3 times continuously OR --&gt; Counter value is repeated in the last 3 consecutive messages OR - During normal communication between sending node and receiving node, Counter = 0x0F repeats 3 times continuously </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1096557945">
DTC shall not be set if all the conditions below are met and last for 1 period - Check Sum is correct - Counter maximum difference (MaxDeltaCounterInit)  = 1 - The Counter value is not repeated - During normal communication between sending node and receiving node, Counter = 0x0F does not appear </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1376656762">FID_LCA_Critical_Impact FID_LCC_Critical_Impact FID_AHB_Critical_Impact FID_ACC_High_Impact FID_ISA_Critical_Impact FID_TSR_Critical_Impact FID_TLR_Critical_Impact FID_AEB_FCW_Medium FID_VRU_FCW_Medium FID_LTAP_FCW_Medium FID_ESA_Critical_Impact FID_LKA_Critical_Impact FID_LCW_Critical_Impact</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_2136608204">40 Drive cycle </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1231760309">1. The ECU/module is gone to sleep 2. Ethernet error 3. Associated ECU Fault</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_253719004">Features that rely on FCM data are not functioning or degraded</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_ADAS.BV.BV_ADAS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTCC21B409">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCC21B409</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>6403081</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>C21B409</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_344837261">Fan Controller Failure</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1537941729">
Check at next stop</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1670728461">1. Reconnect the battery 2. Check the wire harness and connectors 3. Check the ECU 4. If problem persists, replace the ECU</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1681964218">EC 1- Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V)   
EC 2- BCM_PwrMod == IGN ON(0x2)||RUN(0x4)
EC 3-  BUS physical status  
EC 4- De-bounce timer
- ECU Temperature &gt;= 85 Deg C</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1242778992">
50 ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_247768277">
Hydra3_component shall set the DTC If the following condition is TRUE: - For 9V to 13V, if the expected RPM is out of range (Range is 7900 RPM + 20% to 4900 RPM - 20%)
 
Note: 1. Fan Speed Monitor 1 will be used to trigger DTC for Fan Control
 
2. The RPM for the Fan is not controlled by Duty cycle. As per discussions with SW, we have a fixed duty cycle and as such there are multiple parameters for deriving speed calculations. The above range has been chosen considering the Rated Fan speeds for 8 to 13.8 V which should provide a safe range for DTC maturation.
</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1574279607">Hydra3_component shall Not set a DTC if Fan is in Normal operation i.e. Power supply and Fan speed is within Normal range.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1356696783">
After 40 Drive cycle fault will be aged</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_531100593">1. Power supply failure 2. Connection error 3. Harness fault 4. ECU fault</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_849435653">TBD</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                            </DTCS>
                        </DTC-DOP>
                    </DTC-DOPS>
